pelt_args=-i -o autocd
tr_by=hand
why=pelt#49, ruling #113: pelt -i -o autocd starts with the option on (as bash -O autocd and zsh -o autocd start with theirs), set +o lists it on, and set +o autocd turns it off again: the directory is then not found (127). That a shell that is not interactive ignores the option, -c included, is simple/autocd_script's (an interactive pelt's $0 is pelt, so a session cannot start one). Written by hand
